<p><strong>The concept:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is a script<br />
SCP-XXXX embeds itself in online multiplayer games<br />
SCP-XXXX is uneditable or deletable<br />
SCP-XXXX generates a fictitious user account: SCP-XXXX-1<br />
SCP-XXXX-1 always possesses the same username<br />
SCP-XXXX-1 is mostly in-active (or AFK), but will randomly enter short “active” states<br />
During “active” states, SCP-XXXX-1 is capable of communication and seems to innately know each players interests. Having conversations about said topics.<br />
Players who interact with SCP-XXXX-1 will develop a desire to frequent and talk with it, claiming “he is fun to talk to” and “he understands me”.<br />
Players will start prioritising surveying SCP-XXXX-1 for it’s next “active” state over important self needs, such as, consumption of victuals, socialising, sleep, etc.<br />
Players will show signs of stress and violence when deprived of contact with SCP-XXXX-1.<br />
Players exposed for longer than 100 hours will express dysphoria<br />
SCP-XXXX-1 has yet to kill or influence the death of any victim, but can inflict heavy irreversible physical and psychological damage.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>While the concept sounds doable, there isn't much on its purpose or what its end goal is. The skip doesn't seem to aiming for anything particular, which makes the concept (and the narrative to an extent) feel a bit flat/directionless to me.</p>
<p><strong>The narrative:</strong><br />
As for the narrative;</p>
<p>There doesn't really seem to be a clear progression shown here, the structure of the article is laid out (which at this point I would really say is necessary). But the actual events and characters aren't really covered in enough detail to get invested emotionally (or become invested in the skip). Currently the narrative just sort of says there are interviews, or says who the characters are, but there isn't anything showing what they actually learn or what everything is building up to. whats the main conflict? what will make me invested in the characters?-what is their main arc and how do they change? whats the payoff? how will all of this make me as the reader feel?</p>
<p>Quickly noting; its a bit odd how the Foundation found the skip so easily, it doesn't really sound like they had any real way to know if the skip was anomalous, with no prior information.-its a quiet subtle if you don't look in the right places.</p>
<p><strong>Red or green?</strong><br />
Due to may fore mentioned concerns, no-greenlight.</p>
<p>If you would like me review this (or any concept) further, then please feel free to send me a PM or ask via IRC. Response times generally range from 2-12 hours over PMs. If your looking for additional critiques/perspectives in general, then I would highly recommend contacting the butterfly squad :)</p>
